WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.130
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.230 --> 00:01.300
I'm begging you.

3
00:01.300 --> 00:02.870
Can you let him go for now?

4
00:02.870 --> 00:04.700
I told you I didn't kill him.

5
00:04.700 --> 00:06.560
How could I hurt the person I love most?

6
00:06.560 --> 00:07.920
Where did you get these earbuds?

7
00:07.920 --> 00:09.280
I bought them from an online shop.

8
00:09.280 --> 00:10.330
Is it this one?

9
00:10.330 --> 00:11.450
We've got stuff from...

10
00:11.450 --> 00:13.360
Yeah, they're live right now.

11
00:13.360 --> 00:15.466
The jacket the vendor is wearing...

12
00:15.466 --> 00:17.160
I bought it for Anda.

13
00:17.160 --> 00:18.160
Where did you get this jacket?

14
00:18.160 --> 00:20.410
From the dead man's car, right?

15
00:20.410 --> 00:24.920
Dad, who did you sell the dead man's phone and laptop to?

16
00:24.920 --> 00:28.910
​Those things are with someone we should stay far away from.

17
00:28.910 --> 00:31.580
Sir, please buy some cupcakes.

18
00:31.580 --> 00:33.800
Eat something first, then I'll buy your cupcakes.

19
00:37.400 --> 00:40.106
You deserve a reward when you do something good.

20
00:40.106 --> 00:41.480
Do you want anything?

21
00:41.480 --> 00:43.380
I'll get it for you.

22
00:43.380 --> 00:44.920
I can buy it myself.

23
00:44.920 --> 00:48.370
But I'm sure there's something that you really want

24
00:48.370 --> 00:50.740
but money can't buy.

25
00:50.740 --> 00:53.800
I don't care whether or not you like Jinna.

26
00:53.800 --> 00:57.200
He doesn't belong to anyone yet, so let's compete to win him over.

27
00:57.200 --> 00:58.300
Deal?

28
01:05.330 --> 01:10.336
So do you still have practice today?

29
01:10.960 --> 01:13.340
I'll probably practice for a bit more.

30
01:14.425 --> 01:16.440
How many hours have you practiced already?

31
01:16.440 --> 01:20.300
I think it'll be over soon.

32
01:20.300 --> 01:22.653
So, about another hour?

33
01:23.690 --> 01:27.790
Do you know what the concept for our college photo shoot is?

34
01:27.790 --> 01:30.180
I don't know, Risa. Give me a second, I...

35
01:30.180 --> 01:31.760
I know it, though.

36
01:31.760 --> 01:34.750
I'd better not tell you yet. It'll be a surprise.

37
01:34.750 --> 01:37.800
The student council said you and I are perfect together.

38
01:37.800 --> 01:41.360
They said our chemistry is great. They're exaggerating.

39
01:42.790 --> 01:44.000
What did I do to deserve this?

40
01:44.000 --> 01:46.033
Why do I have to watch them get all lovey-dovey?

41
01:48.270 --> 01:51.490
How do you feel about being paired with me?

42
01:51.490 --> 01:54.130
Well, it's good.

43
01:54.130 --> 01:56.510
Sorry, I have to go.

44
01:56.510 --> 01:57.098
Hey...

45
01:57.098 --> 02:00.040
Risa!

46
02:00.040 --> 02:01.470
What are you doing here?

47
02:01.470 --> 02:04.260
I'm here to see Jinna.

48
02:04.260 --> 02:06.068
- Here? - Yeah.

49
02:13.040 --> 02:17.420
[Characters, places, and incidents in this production]

50
02:17.420 --> 02:18.864
[are entirely fictitious.]

51
02:18.864 --> 02:21.630
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

52
03:45.720 --> 03:47.280
Can we talk?

53
03:47.280 --> 03:48.500
About what?

54
03:49.680 --> 03:50.980
About us.

55
03:53.410 --> 03:55.573
I don't have any feelings for Risa.

56
03:56.480 --> 03:58.560
Whatever you think has nothing to do with me.

57
03:58.560 --> 04:00.544
We're just pretending to flirt, remember?

58
04:00.544 --> 04:02.553
It's not like we're actually flirting.

59
04:04.570 --> 04:06.650
Does it look like I'm pretending?

60
04:07.680 --> 04:09.440
I like you.

61
04:09.440 --> 04:10.893
Can't you tell?

62
04:14.960 --> 04:16.333
Dork.

63
04:26.920 --> 04:28.680
I like you.

64
04:28.680 --> 04:30.853
Can't you tell?

65
04:30.853 --> 04:31.920
Dork.

66
04:31.920 --> 04:33.286
Dork.

67
05:06.880 --> 05:11.680
[Jinna: Tell me when you're done with the exam. I'll come to your faculty.]

68
05:18.760 --> 05:22.000
I've looked all over the mall and haven't found anything.

69
05:22.000 --> 05:26.240
Right, they might've been smuggled to the border by now.

70
05:26.240 --> 05:28.250
It's possible.

71
05:28.250 --> 05:32.720
But I hope we'll find either Anda's laptop or his phone.

72
05:34.560 --> 05:37.720
But that security guard was really suspicious.

73
05:37.720 --> 05:42.320
We just asked where he sold it, but why couldn't he tell us?

74
05:42.320 --> 05:43.480
Yeah.

75
05:43.480 --> 05:46.120
What do you think we'll find on Anda's phone?

76
05:47.730 --> 05:49.350
I don't know.

77
05:49.350 --> 05:55.328
But I think he definitely had things he hadn't told anyone, not even us.

78
06:01.000 --> 06:02.080
I'd better go.

79
06:02.080 --> 06:04.340
What? Where are you going now?

80
06:04.340 --> 06:05.600
To pick up Podduang.

81
06:05.600 --> 06:09.760
Yeah, I guess you don't want us anymore. We're strays now?

82
06:09.760 --> 06:12.400
You have always been.

83
06:12.400 --> 06:13.680
Woof-woof.

84
06:14.960 --> 06:16.950
Tod, paw.

85
06:16.950 --> 06:19.010
That's complete nonsense.

86
06:23.670 --> 06:25.500
Why the long face? Cheer up, man.

87
06:25.500 --> 06:27.470
- I'm fine. - After that exam...

88
06:29.280 --> 06:30.340
You're going to fail.

89
06:30.340 --> 06:34.090
- What? You said I'm failing? - You definitely are.

90
06:34.090 --> 06:36.240
Before you fail, I might fall.

91
06:36.240 --> 06:38.756
Come here. I'll teach you a lesson.

92
06:50.510 --> 06:52.470
Jinna?

93
06:52.470 --> 06:54.190
Jinna.

94
06:54.190 --> 06:56.224
See you, Dunk.

95
06:56.224 --> 06:57.479
Jinna!

96
06:58.624 --> 06:59.966
Jinna!

97
07:01.408 --> 07:02.970
Hey.

98
07:02.970 --> 07:04.680
I'm tired.

99
07:04.680 --> 07:05.973
Jinna.

100
07:06.940 --> 07:08.240
Jinna!

101
07:13.080 --> 07:15.120
- What's wrong with you? - Nothing.

102
07:15.120 --> 07:17.200
Don't act like this with me.

103
07:17.200 --> 07:20.280
Tell me if you're mad about something so I'll know and apologize.

104
07:21.490 --> 07:23.160
Are you sure you will?

105
07:24.180 --> 07:25.666
Well, tell me first.

106
07:26.880 --> 07:27.980
Do you still like him?

107
07:27.980 --> 07:29.670
Who?

108
07:29.670 --> 07:31.136
Your best friend.

109
07:31.806 --> 07:33.120
You mean Dunk?

110
07:33.120 --> 07:34.470
I've been over him for ages.

111
07:34.470 --> 07:36.993
Dunk and Bum are basically my parents now.

112
07:37.780 --> 07:39.792
Are you sure you're over him?

113
07:39.792 --> 07:41.140
I am.

114
07:41.140 --> 07:42.890
I even think his face is funny.

115
07:42.890 --> 07:44.960
So you're mad just because of this?

116
07:44.960 --> 07:46.270
That's nonsense.

117
07:46.270 --> 07:48.540
- Well, you... - What?

118
07:48.540 --> 07:50.150
You were so touchy-feely with him.

119
07:50.150 --> 07:52.273
I've always been like this.

120
07:57.360 --> 07:58.446
Let go of me.

121
08:00.560 --> 08:03.870
I understand, but you're with me now.

122
08:03.870 --> 08:05.786
How can you be like that with others?

123
08:07.820 --> 08:11.590
If you want to be touchy-feely, just do it with me.

124
08:11.590 --> 08:12.926
Okay?

125
08:13.680 --> 08:15.640
Jinna.

126
08:15.640 --> 08:17.353
I'm serious, Podduang.

127
08:19.710 --> 08:22.140
Should we take this more seriously?

128
08:22.140 --> 08:24.200
I really like you.

129
08:24.200 --> 08:25.870
I was so damn jealous.

130
08:25.870 --> 08:27.680
I'm crazy about you.

131
08:31.440 --> 08:32.840
Why so quiet?

132
08:33.904 --> 08:35.360
You're blushing, aren't you?

133
08:35.360 --> 08:38.120
Who wouldn't? There are so many people around.

134
08:41.810 --> 08:43.410
No one is looking.

135
08:44.340 --> 08:45.880
Fine, you can let go now.

136
08:45.880 --> 08:47.150
You still haven't answered me.

137
08:47.150 --> 08:48.280
Answer what?

138
08:48.280 --> 08:50.330
Hey, I asked you a question.

139
08:51.840 --> 08:54.890
I already told you that there's nothing between Dunk and me.

140
08:54.890 --> 08:58.050
- I don't have feelings for him anymore. - Not that question.

141
08:58.660 --> 09:00.360
What question, then?

142
09:01.480 --> 09:03.080
Let go. I told you to let go.

143
09:03.080 --> 09:05.960
I asked if we should take this more seriously.

144
09:05.960 --> 09:07.706
If you don't answer, I won't let go.

145
09:12.120 --> 09:14.160
Fine, let's do it then.

146
09:16.310 --> 09:18.480
Everyone's looking.

147
09:18.480 --> 09:20.520
Just look at me.

148
09:20.520 --> 09:22.280
- Let me go. - What?

149
09:40.880 --> 09:42.640
Is this your aunt's house?

150
09:43.466 --> 09:46.646
I'm renting a house from her. I'm close to her.

151
09:48.760 --> 09:50.260
You're here?

152
09:50.260 --> 09:52.230
Let's eat.

153
09:52.230 --> 09:55.160
I missed you so much. Give me a hug.

154
09:55.160 --> 09:56.466
All right.

155
09:59.390 --> 10:01.290
You're Podduang, right?

156
10:01.290 --> 10:04.340
Jinna mentioned you'd be coming along.

157
10:04.340 --> 10:07.060
Yes. Hello, Auntie Amphon.

158
10:07.060 --> 10:09.320
No need to be formal.

159
10:09.320 --> 10:12.046
You must be tired. Let me go get the soup first.

160
10:12.820 --> 10:16.280
Auntie, you don't have to. I'll handle it myself.

161
10:22.190 --> 10:25.060
That's just how Jinna is. He's more about actions than words.

162
10:25.060 --> 10:27.080
Let's have a seat. You must be tired.

163
10:27.080 --> 10:28.420
Come on, dear.

164
10:28.420 --> 10:30.560
Please.

165
10:34.840 --> 10:36.240
How have you been?

166
10:36.240 --> 10:39.010
Jinna didn't force you to come, did he?

167
10:39.632 --> 10:44.560
You seem like the type who gets talked into things easily.

168
10:45.870 --> 10:49.190
He didn't force me. He actually asked me to come.

169
10:49.190 --> 10:52.680
He told me he often has dinner with you.

170
10:52.680 --> 10:54.250
That's right.

171
10:54.250 --> 10:57.700
He comes here pretty often, so I won't get lonely.

172
11:07.630 --> 11:09.880
This is my son, Peera.

173
11:09.880 --> 11:12.640
And this is his family.

174
11:16.910 --> 11:19.280
Your granddaughter is so cute.

175
11:19.280 --> 11:21.306
How old is she?

176
11:22.800 --> 11:25.253
Didn't Jinna tell you?

177
11:27.080 --> 11:28.573
About what?

178
11:32.340 --> 11:34.640
Last year,

179
11:34.640 --> 11:36.973
Peera and his family...

180
11:38.040 --> 11:41.480
were in an accident and passed away.

181
11:41.480 --> 11:43.526
I lost them all.

182
11:48.160 --> 11:50.120
I'm sorry for your loss.

183
11:50.900 --> 11:53.640
I'm sorry for asking about them.

184
11:53.640 --> 11:55.000
It's okay.

185
11:55.000 --> 11:59.293
It's nice that Jinna and his friends come to keep me company.

186
12:01.460 --> 12:04.720
If it weren't for these kids, I don't know...

187
12:05.440 --> 12:09.073
how I'd go on.

188
12:11.473 --> 12:13.395
Jinna has a sixth sense.

189
12:13.395 --> 12:17.666
He heard someone calling for help, so he went in to help.

190
12:17.666 --> 12:19.530
He ended up getting injured

191
12:19.530 --> 12:22.993
and had to stop playing sports for a year because of that incident.

192
12:34.040 --> 12:36.000
That day...

193
12:36.870 --> 12:40.950
I couldn't save her son, so I've been feeling guilty.

194
12:40.950 --> 12:44.592
I've got some sweet pomelo, guys.

195
12:44.592 --> 12:46.750
Here.

196
12:46.750 --> 12:48.106
Thanks, Auntie.

197
12:50.200 --> 12:54.160
Jinna, when you leave, make sure to lock the door.

198
12:54.160 --> 12:56.310
But if you want to stay overnight, that's fine, too.

199
12:56.310 --> 12:59.090
I've already prepared the pillows and blankets for you.

200
12:59.090 --> 13:00.890
Got it, Auntie.

201
13:00.890 --> 13:02.320
I'm going to bed now.

202
13:02.320 --> 13:03.490
Okay. Goodbye.

203
13:03.490 --> 13:04.680
- Goodbye. - Have a good night.

204
13:04.680 --> 13:06.340
All right, I will.

205
13:12.300 --> 13:15.630
You seem really close to her.

206
13:16.460 --> 13:20.288
She's all alone, so I come to see her often.

207
13:21.060 --> 13:24.886
You always carry everyone's burdens, don't you?

208
13:25.900 --> 13:27.133
What do you mean?

209
13:28.260 --> 13:30.930
I mean, everything.

210
13:32.520 --> 13:34.120
You seem to...

211
13:34.973 --> 13:38.013
love taking care of others and doing things for them.

212
13:39.070 --> 13:40.770
To the point where you...

213
13:42.800 --> 13:45.360
put yourself last.

214
13:48.730 --> 13:50.680
You can be weak sometimes, Jinna.

215
14:07.920 --> 14:11.800
For those who matter, I can do anything.

216
14:17.670 --> 14:19.620
I can do anything for you, too.

217
14:21.740 --> 14:23.216
I know.

218
14:25.586 --> 14:27.730
But could you not overexert yourself?

219
14:29.790 --> 14:31.760
I get it.

220
14:31.760 --> 14:33.640
But...

221
14:33.640 --> 14:36.110
I'll find out what happened to Anda first.

222
14:46.080 --> 14:48.880
Why is it so complicated and mysterious?

223
14:48.880 --> 14:51.153
There are only questions without answers.

224
14:52.126 --> 14:55.953
It'd be great if the mysterious earbuds could answer everything we want to know.

225
15:01.520 --> 15:02.880
By the way...

226
15:06.590 --> 15:10.660
Where did that vendor in the livestream get the earbuds from?

227
15:22.050 --> 15:24.800
Are you sure you got them from the security guard?

228
15:24.800 --> 15:25.980
I told you already.

229
15:25.980 --> 15:28.710
That guard actually sold them to me.

230
15:28.710 --> 15:34.100
He always has things to sell me, so I put them in boxes and resold them.

231
15:34.100 --> 15:35.630
I'll talk to him myself.

232
15:35.630 --> 15:36.759
Bye.

233
15:38.840 --> 15:42.240
So, the earbuds Dunk bought from that page...

234
15:43.460 --> 15:46.910
were they really from this security guard?

235
15:47.760 --> 15:50.000
Yes, that's what the vendor said.

236
15:50.000 --> 15:52.806
Just the earbuds, though. No laptop or phone.

237
15:52.806 --> 15:58.430
That means both Anda's jacket and earbuds...

238
15:58.430 --> 16:01.620
were sold to that page by this security guard.

239
16:01.620 --> 16:05.120
That is why I'm here to ask him.

240
16:16.320 --> 16:17.970
Why are you here again?

241
16:19.000 --> 16:22.653
What else did you take from Anda's car besides the jacket?

242
16:24.920 --> 16:26.280
These earbuds, too?

243
16:34.820 --> 16:38.380
I thought they might be worth something, so I took them, too.

244
16:38.380 --> 16:41.440
But that kid only gave me a few coins.

245
16:41.440 --> 16:43.660
I didn't get much at all.

246
16:44.740 --> 16:46.750
They really belonged to Anda.

247
16:56.784 --> 16:59.840
[The Lux Asset]

248
17:27.010 --> 17:29.130
Who did this to you, Anda?

249
17:32.010 --> 17:34.179
Who did this to you?

250
17:43.650 --> 17:45.088
Let's go.

251
18:05.430 --> 18:07.040
Are you okay?

252
18:11.940 --> 18:13.360
Jinna.

253
18:14.430 --> 18:15.872
Yeah.

254
18:21.150 --> 18:23.720
Wait, that car looks familiar.

255
18:37.770 --> 18:39.190
It's Amp.

256
18:41.013 --> 18:42.880
I'm not seeing things, am I?

257
18:45.000 --> 18:46.840
Amp?

258
18:46.840 --> 18:48.333
Your next-door neighbor?

259
18:50.250 --> 18:51.873
What now?

260
18:53.740 --> 18:55.206
How do they know each other?

261
18:56.400 --> 18:57.860
- I don't know. - Take it.

262
18:59.620 --> 19:01.380
I think it looks suspicious.

263
19:26.570 --> 19:28.390
Are you sure?

264
19:28.390 --> 19:31.140
Won't it look like we're being nosy?

265
19:31.140 --> 19:32.550
Trust me, Podduang.

266
19:32.550 --> 19:35.830
If something feels off, we shouldn't ignore it.

267
19:35.830 --> 19:39.040
But Amp? What does she have to do with this?

268
19:39.040 --> 19:40.780
We'll find out soon enough.

269
19:49.860 --> 19:51.640
Is something wrong, Podduang?

270
19:53.800 --> 19:56.290
I just haven't seen you around much lately,

271
19:56.290 --> 19:58.440
so I thought I'd check in on you.

272
19:58.440 --> 20:00.670
Are you doing okay?

273
20:00.670 --> 20:04.700
Yeah, I'm fine. I was just sleeping.

274
20:04.700 --> 20:06.613
I've been working from home.

275
20:09.000 --> 20:10.530
Are you with someone, Amp?

276
20:10.530 --> 20:11.920
Jinna.

277
20:14.060 --> 20:16.373
If that's all, I'll talk to you later.

278
20:18.670 --> 20:22.673
If you need anything, you can find Podduang next door.

279
20:27.260 --> 20:28.940
How could you ask her that?

280
20:28.940 --> 20:30.210
It's personal.

281
20:30.210 --> 20:32.240
Couldn't you tell something was off?

282
20:32.240 --> 20:34.070
She looked like she'd been hurt.

283
20:39.366 --> 20:40.940
Aren't you tired?

284
20:40.940 --> 20:42.659
Go home and get some sleep.

285
20:43.640 --> 20:46.506
No, I want to be with you.

286
20:47.610 --> 20:49.100
Come on.

287
20:49.100 --> 20:50.690
It's piping hot.

288
20:52.520 --> 20:54.030
Want some?

289
20:54.030 --> 20:55.560
- Want it? - Sure.

290
20:56.590 --> 20:58.540
Jinna, have you seen this?

291
20:58.540 --> 21:00.740
The lead actor is so handsome.

292
21:00.740 --> 21:01.910
I haven't seen it.

293
21:01.910 --> 21:03.113
Let's watch it.

294
21:04.080 --> 21:05.410
Okay.

295
21:05.410 --> 21:08.100
You're so nice, unlike my brother.

296
21:08.100 --> 21:11.080
He never watches anything with me.

297
21:11.080 --> 21:14.520
And lately, he's been looking stressed every day.

298
21:14.520 --> 21:15.520
I don't know what's wrong with him.

299
21:15.520 --> 21:16.980
Seeing you makes me sad.

300
21:16.980 --> 21:19.250
Relax, come on.

301
21:27.312 --> 21:28.768
Stop.

302
21:30.992 --> 21:32.608
No.

303
21:36.110 --> 21:37.830
What's wrong, Podduang?

304
21:37.830 --> 21:39.248
Nothing.

305
21:52.140 --> 21:53.296
Satang.

306
21:53.296 --> 21:55.940
What are you doing? You're making a mess.

307
21:55.940 --> 21:58.753
I'm cleaning it up. Stop complaining.

308
22:16.410 --> 22:18.173
Wait, there's more?

309
22:21.630 --> 22:22.660
- Satang. - Yes?

310
22:22.660 --> 22:24.170
Over there, too.

311
23:01.790 --> 23:04.340
Why are you going that way?

312
23:04.340 --> 23:06.940
Come on, it's just a few minutes. You always take shortcuts.

313
23:06.940 --> 23:09.730
But this way is faster.

314
23:09.730 --> 23:12.860
You'll just end up in small alleys, and it'll take even longer.

315
23:13.700 --> 23:16.250
If we get there early, we'll have more time.

316
23:16.250 --> 23:18.520
No, let's go this way.

317
23:18.520 --> 23:21.240
Dunk, let's go this way.

318
23:23.820 --> 23:25.680
Bum, hold this for me.

319
23:25.680 --> 23:26.926
Sure thing.

320
23:27.940 --> 23:29.730
Keep going straight.

321
23:33.650 --> 23:36.613
Come on, let's go this way.

322
23:40.045 --> 23:42.690
Jinna is kinda fussy, isn't he?

323
23:42.690 --> 23:44.380
Don't say that.

324
23:44.380 --> 23:47.740
He just wants to take care of Podduang.

325
23:54.970 --> 23:58.320
Jinna may seem calm and solid like a rock,

326
23:58.320 --> 24:00.944
but he seems to like you a lot, Podduang.

327
24:01.680 --> 24:04.250
See, Dunk's been observing him all along.

328
24:04.250 --> 24:06.368
We totally ship you guys.

329
24:07.930 --> 24:10.600
You guys are so nosy.

330
24:11.220 --> 24:15.800
Well, of course. People's business is mine, too.

331
24:19.510 --> 24:22.780
By the way, what are Art and Tod like?

332
24:22.780 --> 24:25.650
I feel like they're a bit eccentric, maybe?

333
24:26.620 --> 24:27.960
You'll find out later.

334
24:27.960 --> 24:29.970
That's why I asked you guys to come along.

335
24:29.970 --> 24:32.310
Jinna said he wanted us all to get close.

336
24:32.310 --> 24:34.650
- No. - Hey!

337
24:34.650 --> 24:37.233
Jinna is so smooth.

338
24:57.170 --> 24:59.370
Sit in a better position if you're going to sleep.

339
24:59.370 --> 25:01.733
You're going to hurt your neck sleeping like that.

340
25:05.080 --> 25:08.560
"You're going to hurt your neck sleeping like that."

341
25:10.310 --> 25:13.520
You two are seriously too much.

342
25:13.520 --> 25:16.960
Your voice is so soft when you talk to Podduang.

343
25:17.530 --> 25:18.810
I'm using my normal voice.

344
25:18.810 --> 25:21.880
Look at that. Talk about double standards.

345
25:21.880 --> 25:22.946
Soft...

346
25:23.800 --> 25:28.650
Come on, Tod, we're just his best friends.

347
25:28.650 --> 25:30.060
Do you know who he is?

348
25:31.130 --> 25:34.190
His sweetheart.

349
25:37.320 --> 25:40.520
Dunk, I'll drive back.

350
25:40.520 --> 25:42.820
- Jeez. - You jerk.

351
25:42.820 --> 25:46.280
Don't pretend to be shy. I know.

352
25:46.280 --> 25:49.120
On the way back, you'll have someone sitting next to you.

353
25:49.120 --> 25:51.576
- Who? - Who could it be?

354
25:52.800 --> 25:55.552
My sweetheart will be sitting next to me. You happy now?

355
25:56.830 --> 25:59.033
- "Sweetheart"? - "Sweetheart"?

356
26:02.900 --> 26:04.670
Don't try to run away from us.

357
26:04.670 --> 26:07.400
We're like wandering spirits, following you everywhere.

358
26:07.400 --> 26:11.240
I'll have Dunk drop both of you right here if you don't shut your mouths.

359
26:24.300 --> 26:25.553
Move it.

360
26:29.740 --> 26:30.810
Hurry.

361
26:30.810 --> 26:33.240
Art, it's so cool in here.

362
26:33.240 --> 26:34.866
Damn, an arcade.

363
26:37.790 --> 26:40.060
This is such a classic.

364
26:41.240 --> 26:44.066
Damn, this house is huge, though.

365
26:44.066 --> 26:45.540
Who booked this?

366
26:45.540 --> 26:47.440
I did. I got it cheap, too.

367
26:47.440 --> 26:48.613
Impressive?

368
26:50.240 --> 26:52.600
You're the best.

369
26:52.600 --> 26:55.480
You're not only pretty but also smart.

370
26:55.480 --> 26:56.620
Hey.

371
26:56.620 --> 26:59.080
Her boyfriend is sitting right there, man.

372
26:59.080 --> 27:00.920
Jeez, you idiot!

373
27:00.920 --> 27:02.170
I was just complimenting her.

374
27:02.170 --> 27:04.520
It doesn't mean I like everyone I compliment.

375
27:04.520 --> 27:05.760
Look at Jinna.

376
27:05.760 --> 27:08.353
I say he's handsome every day. As if I like him that much.

377
27:09.930 --> 27:12.390
So, how are we splitting the bedrooms?

378
27:12.390 --> 27:14.330
There are three rooms, so it's perfect, right?

379
27:14.330 --> 27:17.400
Dunk and I will share one. What about you guys?

380
27:17.400 --> 27:21.860
Art and I will share one since we're roommates anyway.

381
27:22.640 --> 27:23.980
And...

382
27:24.660 --> 27:27.835
I... I prefer to sleep alone.

383
27:27.835 --> 27:29.520
I'll just sleep on the couch.

384
27:29.520 --> 27:31.710
Wait, why would you do that?

385
27:31.710 --> 27:33.446
You can just share a room with Jinna.

386
27:34.220 --> 27:35.400
I'm good.

387
27:35.400 --> 27:37.290
I'm worried I won't be able to sleep.

388
27:37.880 --> 27:40.280
You can put your stuff in the room first.

389
27:40.280 --> 27:41.400
I'll sleep out here.

390
27:41.400 --> 27:44.240
I'll sleep on the couch.

391
27:44.240 --> 27:46.166
Just put your stuff in the room.

392
27:49.300 --> 27:50.880
We're going to pick our room first.

393
27:50.880 --> 27:52.560
See you, guys.

394
27:54.146 --> 27:57.470
I'll put your stuff inside for you.

395
27:57.470 --> 27:59.320
It's okay. I'll do it myself.

396
27:59.320 --> 28:01.580
- It's okay. Let me help. - It's okay.

397
28:01.580 --> 28:03.560
I can do it myself.

398
28:20.704 --> 28:22.560
What's everyone doing outside?

399
28:22.560 --> 28:24.900
Art and Tod are heading to the beach.

400
28:25.560 --> 28:28.310
Yeah, go ahead. It's still hot outside.

401
28:28.310 --> 28:30.040
I'll be there when it's cooler.

402
28:31.980 --> 28:34.160
You haven't slept with Jinna yet, have you?

403
28:34.160 --> 28:36.080
What kind of question is that?

404
28:36.080 --> 28:39.800
Come on, don't play innocent. It's natural.

405
28:39.800 --> 28:41.373
We haven't done anything yet.

406
28:42.000 --> 28:44.240
We're not even dating yet.

407
28:44.240 --> 28:45.620
I knew it.

408
28:45.620 --> 28:47.300
Why are you so awkward around him?

409
28:47.300 --> 28:49.320
Why are you so shy?

410
28:49.930 --> 28:52.500
What do you mean? I'm not shy.

411
28:52.500 --> 28:53.700
You're not?

412
28:53.700 --> 28:55.630
Then why can't you share a room with him?

413
28:55.630 --> 28:57.790
Why should I do it, though?

414
28:57.790 --> 28:59.310
Because you should be able to!

415
28:59.310 --> 29:01.180
But why?

416
29:01.180 --> 29:03.460
Jeez, just share a room with him.

417
29:03.460 --> 29:06.210
This doesn't happen every day, you know.

418
29:09.920 --> 29:11.260
You're so nosy.

419
29:11.260 --> 29:13.600
Do you not want a boyfriend?

420
29:13.600 --> 29:15.680
- None of your business. - Hey!

421
29:16.680 --> 29:18.266
I'm just clearing the way for you.

422
29:26.192 --> 29:27.910
Don't follow me!

423
29:27.910 --> 29:29.060
Tod!

424
29:31.970 --> 29:34.020
Your friends are so funny.

425
29:36.430 --> 29:39.510
Bum said Tod and Art are so eccentric.

426
29:41.730 --> 29:43.640
What about me?

427
29:43.640 --> 29:45.600
Am I not funny?

428
29:45.600 --> 29:46.813
Let go of me.

429
29:52.130 --> 29:54.350
My friends love the sea.

430
29:55.050 --> 29:58.050
They always want to come here after exams.

431
30:00.026 --> 30:03.473
But the one who loved it most was probably Anda.

432
30:04.640 --> 30:06.320
He was even counting down the days.

433
30:15.184 --> 30:16.608
Be careful.

434
30:23.344 --> 30:24.800
Tod, stop!

435
30:28.280 --> 30:30.560
We were so happy back then.

436
30:31.200 --> 30:32.510
This should be ready.

437
30:32.510 --> 30:34.480
This one? Looks like it's almost ready.

438
30:36.160 --> 30:37.840
Is that everything? Let's go.

439
30:37.840 --> 30:40.020
- Even when Kum joined us... - I'll bring it over.

440
30:40.020 --> 30:41.550
This semester has been exhausting.

441
30:41.550 --> 30:44.180
- Go help them grill the BBQ. - Everything was still great.

442
30:44.180 --> 30:47.960
- All right, cheers! - Cheers!

443
30:48.530 --> 30:50.233
Take one each, guys.

444
30:51.313 --> 30:57.620
- Thank you for the meal, Kum and Anda. - Thank you so much.

445
30:57.620 --> 31:01.380
Kum, why is this BBQ so sweet?

446
31:01.380 --> 31:04.850
Right, Tod? They shouldn't be adding sugar to BBQ.

447
31:04.850 --> 31:06.906
Is it because the person grilling it is in love?

448
31:07.766 --> 31:09.088
Too bad...

449
31:10.680 --> 31:12.473
We didn't get to come together this year.

450
31:16.620 --> 31:18.480
Sometimes I wonder...

451
31:20.670 --> 31:23.040
what the hell I've gotten myself into.

452
31:25.440 --> 31:27.520
I don't even know how my friend died.

453
31:29.210 --> 31:31.220
Things are getting out of control.

454
31:35.200 --> 31:36.493
Jinna...

455
31:45.386 --> 31:46.920
I'm right here.

456
31:48.733 --> 31:51.190
No matter what happens, I'll be right here with you.

457
32:06.720 --> 32:08.880
- No, I'm not riding on your back. - Come on.

458
32:13.990 --> 32:17.000
- Come on. - There we go.

459
32:35.595 --> 32:37.640
- Hey, look at them. - Hey!

460
32:37.640 --> 32:40.930
- Hey! - What are you two doing?

461
32:40.930 --> 32:42.850
- Get in the sea. - Want to get in the sea?

462
32:42.850 --> 32:45.300
- Want to get in the sea? - No way.

463
32:46.580 --> 32:48.060
Podduang!

464
32:48.060 --> 32:50.393
One, two, three.

465
32:56.320 --> 32:59.480
Do you guys come to the same place every year?

466
32:59.480 --> 33:02.920
Of course. And Art gets drunk like this every year, too.

467
33:04.460 --> 33:07.850
What's up, Art? Does getting drunk make you feel down?

468
33:11.970 --> 33:13.650
I miss Anda.

469
33:17.090 --> 33:19.680
We come here together every year.

470
33:20.586 --> 33:23.010
Being here without him is just...

471
33:24.200 --> 33:26.000
Why did he have to die?

472
33:27.400 --> 33:30.240
Art, that's enough. Stop drinking, man.

473
33:31.773 --> 33:35.800
So what do you guys think about this?

474
33:35.800 --> 33:37.330
Who do you think did it?

475
33:38.473 --> 33:40.600
I don't know who did it yet,

476
33:40.600 --> 33:43.720
but I've got tons of ideas about how they did it.

477
33:44.650 --> 33:45.940
What do you mean?

478
33:45.940 --> 33:49.580
I mean, I want to know how he was killed, too.

479
33:50.226 --> 33:55.152
The footage confirmed that Anda drove there and parked the car all by himself.

480
33:55.740 --> 34:01.344
Even though there's no footage after that, the timing fits with his death.

481
34:02.037 --> 34:04.520
What if the killer struck while the car was parked?

482
34:04.520 --> 34:07.690
Why didn't Anda just open the door and get out?

483
34:07.690 --> 34:11.150
Why would he just fall asleep and suffocate?

484
34:11.150 --> 34:13.710
Right? That's what's suspicious.

485
34:14.290 --> 34:15.850
Guess what?

486
34:15.850 --> 34:20.710
If you modify a car by installing a control unit

487
34:20.710 --> 34:24.150
and connecting it to a phone with just a little setup,

488
34:24.920 --> 34:29.400
it basically becomes a magic remote that lets you control the car.

489
34:29.400 --> 34:30.520
What?

490
34:30.520 --> 34:32.590
There's no way you could do that with a remote.

491
34:32.590 --> 34:34.150
It really is possible.

492
34:34.150 --> 34:38.160
If the car's control unit gets hacked and re-paired,

493
34:38.160 --> 34:42.330
the car can be locked or unlocked by someone outside.

494
34:42.330 --> 34:44.310
You've watched too many movies, Tod.

495
34:44.310 --> 34:46.730
Does that kind of remote really exist?

496
34:46.730 --> 34:48.390
Hey.

497
34:48.390 --> 34:50.530
It's just like a Bluetooth speaker.

498
34:50.530 --> 34:52.460
We're studying mechanical engineering.

499
34:52.460 --> 34:54.153
The professor even mentioned it.

500
34:54.780 --> 34:56.540
I've been thinking about it, too.

501
34:56.540 --> 34:58.410
This could be how he was killed.

502
35:00.040 --> 35:04.480
I think the only way we're going to get anywhere now

503
35:04.480 --> 35:07.986
is to find Anda's laptop or phone.

504
35:08.760 --> 35:10.500
And...

505
35:10.500 --> 35:14.633
Why are you so sure that you'll find something in there?

506
35:15.573 --> 35:17.570
I don't know.

507
35:17.570 --> 35:19.584
I just know we have to find them.

508
35:36.270 --> 35:37.770
Where's the hair dryer?

509
35:39.560 --> 35:42.073
Bum borrowed it this afternoon.

510
35:43.410 --> 35:45.140
She probably forgot to return it.

511
35:46.080 --> 35:47.193
Okay.

512
35:51.140 --> 35:52.592
Jeez.

513
35:53.300 --> 35:56.180
Are you a dog? You got it all over me.

514
35:57.200 --> 36:00.000
My hair is wet. What am I supposed to do?

515
36:01.100 --> 36:03.450
Go sit down. I'll dry it for you.

516
36:14.240 --> 36:16.210
Are you sleepy?

517
36:16.210 --> 36:19.660
Not yet. I need to let my food settle since I ate so much.

518
36:20.310 --> 36:22.060
You ate so much?

519
36:22.060 --> 36:23.920
You barely ate anything.

520
36:23.920 --> 36:27.500
I ate just fine. You're the one who ate a lot.

521
36:27.500 --> 36:30.777
Well, I'm an athlete.

522
36:30.777 --> 36:32.753
It's normal for me to eat a lot.

523
36:34.626 --> 36:38.280
Well, what do you like to eat?

524
36:38.280 --> 36:40.640
You always order fried rice.

525
36:41.440 --> 36:42.900
Railway fried rice.

526
36:44.720 --> 36:45.933
Really?

527
36:54.800 --> 36:56.240
That's such a cute name.

528
36:56.960 --> 36:58.610
Railway fried rice?

529
36:58.610 --> 36:59.953
What's so cute about it?

530
37:02.640 --> 37:05.997
I don't know. It just sounds cute.

531
37:06.700 --> 37:10.112
And when is your birthday?

532
37:10.953 --> 37:12.320
Why are you asking?

533
37:13.120 --> 37:15.760
I just want to get to know you.

534
37:16.950 --> 37:20.432
I was born on Saturday, May fifth.

535
37:21.680 --> 37:23.740
Making it sound complicated?

536
37:25.450 --> 37:27.790
What about you? When's your birthday?

537
37:28.680 --> 37:30.120
I'm not telling you.

538
37:33.500 --> 37:35.366
You're younger than me, aren't you?

539
37:36.120 --> 37:37.920
That's why you're not telling me.

540
37:41.310 --> 37:43.450
Not telling you.

541
37:50.560 --> 37:51.839
Just tell me.

542
37:53.680 --> 37:56.326
Your future boyfriend is going to buy you a gift.

543
38:08.360 --> 38:10.680
Do you not want a boyfriend?

544
38:10.680 --> 38:12.240
I'm just clearing the way for you.

545
39:02.620 --> 39:04.210
Can't sleep?

546
39:05.200 --> 39:06.600
Yeah.

547
39:08.720 --> 39:10.120
The blanket...

548
39:10.120 --> 39:12.050
If it's in the way, you can throw it down here.

549
39:12.050 --> 39:13.740
The AC is blowing right on me.

550
39:18.599 --> 39:20.820
Really? Are you cold?

551
39:22.253 --> 39:23.950
It's not that cold.

552
39:24.620 --> 39:28.330
But you were tossing the blanket around like you were annoyed.

553
39:29.870 --> 39:31.750
I wasn't annoyed.

554
39:31.750 --> 39:33.390
I just couldn't sleep.

555
39:39.010 --> 39:42.976
You can sleep up here if you want.

556
39:48.352 --> 39:49.473
Well...

557
39:50.840 --> 39:53.230
the AC is blowing on you, isn't it?

558
40:12.360 --> 40:15.400
I know you're stressing over what happened to Anda,

559
40:18.693 --> 40:20.270
but I promise...

560
40:21.359 --> 40:23.206
that no matter what happens,

561
40:24.293 --> 40:26.270
I'll always be here for you.

562
40:36.192 --> 40:37.540
Thanks.

563
41:44.440 --> 41:45.980
I'm not messing around this time.

564
41:47.960 --> 41:49.213
What?

565
41:50.546 --> 41:51.700
Get up.

566
45:38.720 --> 45:41.013
The congee is already mushy, man.

567
45:44.010 --> 45:45.780
My friend is even worse.

568
45:48.510 --> 45:49.984
Jinna!

569
45:50.870 --> 45:52.288
Jinna.

570
45:54.080 --> 45:55.500
Jinna!

571
45:56.360 --> 45:57.760
That's mine.

572
45:58.810 --> 46:00.620
Yours is over there.

573
46:04.340 --> 46:08.450
I couldn't sleep a wink last night. It was so freaking loud.

574
46:08.450 --> 46:10.140
No, it wasn't.

575
46:10.140 --> 46:11.460
What?

576
46:11.460 --> 46:14.950
Tod was snoring. That's what I was trying to say.

577
46:14.950 --> 46:17.600
Jeez, before I fell asleep,

578
46:17.600 --> 46:20.880
I heard something that sounded like a cow being slaughtered.

579
46:23.110 --> 46:25.810
What was it? Was something wrong?

580
46:25.810 --> 46:28.540
It's this guy. He always sings when he's drunk.

581
46:28.540 --> 46:30.640
I can handle him singing.

582
46:30.640 --> 46:33.136
But when he sings out of tune, I can't take it.

583
46:39.530 --> 46:42.180
So, how was it for you two?

584
46:44.560 --> 46:45.580
Everything was fine.

585
46:45.580 --> 46:47.280
I slept in my room, and Jinna slept on the couch.

586
46:47.280 --> 46:49.240
It was perfectly fine.

587
46:49.240 --> 46:53.079
I slept on the couch, and Podduang slept in his room.

588
47:06.930 --> 47:09.330
Don't want to date an engineering student?

589
47:09.330 --> 47:11.030
No.

590
47:11.030 --> 47:13.030
Then how about dating a soccer player?

591
47:13.620 --> 47:16.720
You know, Anda was always targeted by haters.

592
47:16.720 --> 47:18.930
There's this one account that's been stirring up all the hate.

593
47:18.930 --> 47:20.700
It must be one of these five people.

594
47:20.700 --> 47:23.860
There's no way Anda would've let himself suffocate in that car.

595
47:23.860 --> 47:26.540
Could it be that someone made him take pills?

596
47:26.540 --> 47:28.300
Or drugged him.

597
47:28.300 --> 47:30.080
Take a deep breath.

598
47:30.080 --> 47:31.710
I've figured out who killed Anda.

599
47:31.710 --> 47:33.232
If Anda was really murdered,

600
47:33.232 --> 47:37.050
then I will bring the killer to justice myself.
